-# The button that applies one of the editor's repairs to the buffer. No local
-# gate: this renders only where the caller has already established there is
-# something to repair.
-#
-# locals:
-#   kind    — which repair to run, read by XmlController#repair
-#   label   — what the button says it does, so each offer names its own fix
-#   variant — the Bootstrap outline colour, matched to the alert it sits in
-#
-# `form:` rather than nesting, because the three places an offer belongs are all
-# outside #raw_xml_form — the refusal banner above it, the advisory below that,
-# and the Turbo-replaced preview pane beside it. A submitter outside a form still
-# fires that form's submit event, so the editor controller still syncs the Ace
-# buffer into the hidden field, and the curator's unsaved edits are what gets
-# repaired.
-#
-# It must stay a Turbo submission. Per-form CSRF tokens bind the form's token to
-# the form's own action, so a `formaction` override can only authenticate on the
-# global token Turbo sends in the X-CSRF-Token header — opting out of Turbo here
-# earns a 422 from InvalidAuthenticityToken. Save relies on the same thing.
%button.btn.btn-sm.mt-2{class: "btn-outline-#{variant}", type: "submit", form: "raw_xml_form", formaction: xml_repair_path(kind: kind)}
  %i.fas.fa-screwdriver-wrench.me-1
  = label
